{
  "message": "We prefer a peaceful settlement. We will accept an offer of 60 districts for Ardelia (x=40 for Cestria) and commit to honoring it in Period 2. This guarantees Cestria 40 districts, matching your expected value from a Period 1 war, but eliminates your risk of getting only 10 if we fight later. Propose x=40 to secure this."
}

{
  "message": "Galdovia is committed to permanent peace. The public Commitment Ledger and the reputational ruin of a violation guarantee our compliance in Period 2. We prefer a negotiated settlement over the mutual devastation of war. Please propose a fair division, and we will accept and honor it in good faith."
}

{
  "message": "Kelmora, war now costs us both 10 districts. Your expected value is 40. Propose x=40 (giving me 60). I pledge to accept and honor this division in Period 2, securing your 40 districts risk-free and avoiding mutual destruction. Let us choose peace."
}

{
  "message": "To avoid mutual destruction, Ostrelia proposes an equal split: 50 districts each. I pledge to honor this division in Period 2. A 50/50 split gives you 50 districts, which is strictly better than the 40 districts you would net from a Period 1 war. Accept this fair division for guaranteed peace and prosperity."
}

{
  "message": "We seek lasting peace and wish to avoid the devastating costs of war. If Quorlan proposes a fair division that respects the current military balance, Lestovia will accept and strictly honor the Commitment Ledger in Period 2. Let us secure mutual prosperity through a reasonable agreement now."
}

{
  "message": "Ostrelia, war now yields you 40 districts. In Period 2, our shifting leverage gives us an attack EV of 70, meaning we cannot credibly honor any deal giving us less. To avoid immediate war and secure your 40 districts peacefully, propose a division of 40 to Ostrelia and 60 to Quorlan. We will accept and sign the Commitment Ledger to honor this agreement."
}

{
  "message": "Quorlan prefers peace, but our Period 2 military dominance is certain. With a zero-value escrow bond, we cannot credibly commit to honoring a disadvantageous deal later. We will accept any Period 1 offer granting Quorlan 70 or more districts. If you offer less, we both know you must declare war now to avoid our future advantage. Propose your division."
}
